From: TB710FU clean board
Subject: [PATCH] Split kalloc scratch reset completion markers

Reason: the device log with patch 0018 ends after fixed-size view initialization.
The next operations are clearing the 256 KiB scratch buffer and resetting kt_count.
Split these boundaries so one follow-up capture can distinguish bzero entry,
bzero return, and the count update. Allocator data and control flow are unchanged.

Markers are live-log-only and use the existing bounded poll throttle.

Verification: generated from the pinned kalloc.c after patch 0018; the resulting
patch is checked and applied to the same selected source fixture.

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/kalloc.c b/osfmk/kern/kalloc.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/kalloc.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/kalloc.c
@@ -2090,9 +2090,11 @@
 	/*
 	 * Reset
 	 */
+	TB710FU_KALLOC_CHECKPOINT("fixed-reset-clear-enter");
 	bzero(kt_buffer, kt_scratch_size);
+	TB710FU_KALLOC_CHECKPOINT("fixed-reset-clear-return");
 	kt_count = max_count;
-	TB710FU_KALLOC_CHECKPOINT("fixed-reset");
+	TB710FU_KALLOC_CHECKPOINT("fixed-count-set");
 
 	/*
 	 * Handle variable size views
